, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff The Horn Laboratory in The BioDiscovery Institute and Department of Biological Sciences at the University of North Texas is seeking to hire a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to join our team. Our lab broadly focuses on characterizing molecular processes and engineering lipid-based bioproducts in plant systems Read more Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Advertising/Marketing Staff The College of Visual Arts and Design (CVAD) at the University of North Texas (UNT) is seeking a Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations to provide strategic leadership for college-level marketing, communications, and public relations. The Director develops and implements an integrated communications strategy that advances the college’s priorities, strengthens its visibility and reputation, and supports student recruitment, engagement, advancement, and community outreach.\nThe Director oversees CVAD communications across multiple platforms and formats, including the college website, social media, newsletters, press releases, advertising, donor and recruitment materials, publications, short-form video, and other print and digital content. The position creates and edits clear, compelling, and audience-focused communications and identifies opportunities to share the accomplishments and impact of CVAD students, faculty, staff, alumni, programs, and partners.\nWorking closely with UNT’s University Brand Strategy and Communications (UBSC), the Director ensures that CVAD communications align with university branding, communication standards, institutional priorities, and applicable policies. The position requires exceptional writing, editing, proofreading, project-management, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines.\nThe Director is responsible for ensuring that web, digital, print, and multimedia communications meet institutional policies and accessibility requirements, including ADA compliance. Additional responsibilities include cultivating media and campus relationships, researching marketing opportunities and best practices, supporting major college events and initiatives, and supervising student employees. Read more Student Media Coordinator Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff It is responsible for supporting multiple student media groups, including the Debate Team, Comm Future Pros, DCTV, Hatch, KNTU, NT Daily, NTTV, and Swoop. This position will perform or assist with a variety of administrative including (1) payroll processes; (2) purchases for student meetings and events; (3) requisition and invoice management; (4) reserve rooms for student media meetings; (5) working with faculty advisors and staff managers of various student media areas; (6) other duties as may be assigned. Read more Digital Accessibility Specialist Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff The Digital Accessibility Specialist within the Office of Disability Access is a student-, faculty-, and staff-facing position focused on advancing digital accessibility across the University of North Texas. The Digital Accessibility Specialist works directly with students with disabilities and faculty to identify, troubleshoot, and resolve digital accessibility barriers that may impact a student’s access to course materials, instructional technologies, or participation in the academic experience. Read more UNT Retail Dining Services, Union Burger- Food Service Specialist Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff The Food Service Specialist at Union Burger within UNT Retail Dining Services is responsible for delivering high-quality food and exceptional customer service in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. This position supports daily operations by preparing and serving menu items, maintaining food safety and sanitation standards, and ensuring a clean and welcoming dining area for students, faculty, staff, and guests. Read more Strategic Communications Coordinator Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Advancement Advancement/Development Staff The Strategic Communications Coordinator supports the successful execution of communications initiatives across the Division of University Advancement by coordinating projects, maintaining departmental workflows, and helping ensure strategic priorities move efficiently from planning through completion. Read more UNT Retail Dining Services, Union Burger - Food Service Supervisor Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff The Food Service Supervisor for Union Burger at the University of North Texas -Retail Dining Services is responsible for overseeing daily restaurant operations, ensuring exceptional customer service, and maintaining high standards of food quality, safety, and cleanliness. This role provides hands-on leadership to team members, supports staff training and development, and ensures efficient workflow during all service periods. Read more Sr Student & Pgrm Coordinator Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Research Administration Staff The position coordinates various activities to recruit, retain, mentor students to support the mission and strategic plan of the academic program. Responsible for managing the daily operations of the program, including mass communications, publications, research and interacting with students and potential students. Supervises all administrative tasks related to strategic planning, travel logistics, and recruiting. This position is essential to providing high quality coaching and training, while nurturing the development of students. Read more Graphic Design Specialist Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Advertising/Marketing Staff This position is responsible for the professional, artistic design and production of impactful graphics and media content for communications and marketing materials of the College of Music, both print and digital. This work supports our efforts to enhance the Colleges reputation, build audiences for our concerts and events, and support the recruitment of our students, faculty, and staff. Read more Asst Dir Registrar Processing Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Enrollment Management Student Finance/Registrar Staff This position is responsible for managing and directing daily operations of Reporting, Systems, and Testing, and overseeing process continuity for the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Contributes to the Office of the Registrar efforts to promote productivity, collaboration, and coordination within and between all sections of the office and functions as an escalation point for highly complex issues including handling advanced exceptions. This role requires direct interaction with students, former students, faculty, and staff, processing data-driven requests, developing training and ensuring compliance with a range of institutional, state, and federal regulations. This position requires a detail driven critical thinker who thrives in a fast-paced environment, is technically proficient in diverse software platforms and understands interdependencies. This position requires discernment and problem-solving to review escalations and complex and collaborative processes. Promotes and generates collaboration across teams to achieve a collective outcome and creates a unified team that get results optimizing outcomes and impact that directly affects enrollment and retention. Read more Senior Academic Counselor Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff This position is responsible for providing counseling to students by appraising their interests, aptitudes, and abilities to develop a career path and degree fit. This role typically provides supervision to lower level staff directly or on a project basis but may serve as an expert or point of escalation for more complex projects or issues. Counsels students on academic pursuits through the completion of degree program; connects students with available resources for academic success and personal/professional development; researches and evaluates and delivers presentations on services provided. This position is responsible for creating and implementing programs related to student success and retention. Read more Associate Registrar Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Enrollment Management Student Finance/Registrar Student Services/Student Affairs Staff This position is responsible for strategic oversight of Curriculum, Scheduling, and Transfer, including planning, organizing, and ensuring continuity and continuous improvement of processes, systems, and student services including the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Involved in new initiatives with colleagues across campus related to enrollment and retention to ensure successful implementation. Oversees operations of multiple functional areas and works directly with staff for ongoing professional development and the implementation of new initiatives, and/or updated systems, policies, and processes. Advises students, parents, faculty and staff about departmental and university regulations. Requires discernment to resolve complex escalations and implement proactive solutions. Read more Sr Lab Animal Technician Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Research & Innovation Research Administration Research Support - Laboratory/Non-Laboratory Staff The Sr Lab Animal Technician provides operational and technical support for the daily functions of the Vivarium Animal Lab. Reporting to and in collaboration with the Research Animal Lab Manager, this position ensures the delivery of high-quality animal care, mentors junior husbandry staff and supports regulatory compliance across institutional and federal standards. This position provides technical expertise and guidance as a resource for supporting all research staff and animal care personnel. Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - Materials Science & Engineering Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff This position is required to work closely with UNT faculty colleagues, and researchers at sponsoring agencies on high performance metallic materials. The position would require strong background in microstructure, mechanical properties, understanding of advanced solid state processing of metallic materials. Experience with solid state additive manufacturing of aluminum alloys is essential. Read more Student Services Coordinator- FSL Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Academic Advising Academic Technician Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Show More Show Less Staff Provides support to student groups within Fraternity and Sorority Life and acts as an advisor and advocate for fraternity/sorority members. The coordinator assists the FSL unit in facilitating event planning, leadership, member development, and risk management, among other topics. The position collaborates with university departments in providing resources to the fraternity and sorority community. Read more Vegan Cook Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff Prepare and serve high-quality plant-based meals for Mean Greens, UNT's nationally acclaimed Vegan certified dining hall and the nation's first and only 100% plant-based collegiate dining hall. Responsible for preparing daily menu items, maintaining an attractive and fully stocked serving line throughout meal service, and ensuring food quality, consistency, and presentation standards are met. Monitor and maintain proper food temperatures using thermometers in accordance with Food Department policies and food safety regulations. Support a varied menu featuring globally inspired vegan cuisine, including stations such as fried rice, Vietnamese pho, Mediterranean grill, and fresh guacamole, while contributing to a positive dining experience for students and guests. Read more Program Dir CVAD Spec Initv Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Fine Arts Staff This position provides strategic and creative leadership for the UNT CVAD Galleries, overseeing exhibitions, programming, collections, operations, and partnerships that support the College’s educational and cultural mission. The position develops and manages a dynamic exhibition program that showcases student, faculty, visiting, and professional artists while engaging the university and broader North Texas communities. Read more Senior Program Project Coordinator Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Advertising/Marketing Staff This role is the operational engine of the Murphy Center's student-facing programs. The Assistant Director manages all aspects of pitch competitions, drives marketing and outreach to maximize participation, and builds the pipeline from classroom to competition to accelerator. A key performance objective is growing the Innovate UNT and Breakthrough Ventures competitions to $100,000+ in total prize money by Year 3 while embedding competition requirements into select courses across campus. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 133 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 › 1155 Union Circle #311277, Denton, Tx 76203-5017 Phone: 855.878.7650 (option #2) HRemployment@untsystem.edu Quick Links Home View All System Jobs My Settings Applicant Login Equal Employment Opportunity | Notice of Nondiscrimination | Title IX | Workplace Posters Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"