tion and adjudication of student conduct cases, which includes high level decision making such as assigning suspensions and expulsions. Additionally, this position maintains on-call responsibilities for responding to student emergencies. Finally, this position assists in prevention and education programming responsibilities related to Care Team and Conduct topics. Read more Student Finance Service Specialist Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Finance Financial Aid Staff This position is responsible for accurately processing student finance transactions and processes daily cash receipts for the institution. This includes maintaining accounting records and preparation of financial reports. Work in collaboration with other administrative departments. Provide guidance regarding student and department accounts. Delivers exceptional customer service to students and their parent. Conduct research and provide reports related to reconciliation issues. Read more Financial Aid Counselor Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Financial Aid Staff Evaluates and analyzes financial information submitted by applicants to determine eligibility for financial assistance and determines type and amount of aid to be awarded in accordance with established federal and university standards and guidelines. Coordinates and administers assigned financial aid programs such as the federal work study program, Pell/SEOG, and state grants. Read more Student Services Coordinator (Center for Academic Performance) Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff The Writing Coordinator in the Center for Academic Performance is a hybrid position, working both on campus and remotely to aid in the support of students by providing academic writing and presentation support. This position will meet individually with students, both in person and via online meeting platforms, to assess and provide feedback regarding writing skills. They will work closely with other departments and academic programs to integrate writing skills with curriculum. They will provide students with presentations and workshops focused on the enhancement of writing skills. When on campus, the Writing Coordinator does work out of a shared office space, with access to space to meet privately with students. Read more Medical Assistant Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Medical Assistants Staff UNT Health Family Medicine is seeking a compassionate Medical Assistant to join our dynamic team of healthcare providers at the University of North Texas Health Science Center. This role requires a candidate with strong organizational skills, a wide set of interests and skill set, and strong interpersonal communication abilities. Candidate must exhibit compassion, understanding, the ability to work well in teams, and the ability to function in a fastpaced environment is critical for this position. Read more Academic Program Manager Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff This Academic Program Manager is responsible for the academic administration, coordination, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of TCOM’s four-year Professional Identity and Health Systems Practice (PIHSP) curriculum. PIHSP is a longitudinal curriculum integrating professional identity formation with Health Systems Science and related competencies across Years 1–4 of medical school. The Academic Program Manager serves as a central operational resource for the Director of PIHSP Course, Director of Health Systems Science, Innovation and Leadership, Chair of Medical Education and Health Systems Science, PISHP course and section directors, PIHSP senior academic program manager, faculty, staff, students, and curriculum leadership.\n\nThe Academic Program Manager coordinates PIHSP components including Ethics, Health Systems Science, Innovation, Patient Safety, Population and Public Health, Interprofessional Education, Health Promotion and Disease Prevention, Health Policy, Health Informatics and Artificial Intelligence, Emotional Intelligence, leadership, and other current and evolving PIHSP content. The employee ensures alignment of activities, objectives, assessments, student experiences, faculty responsibilities, and curricular documentation across all four years. Read more Senior Custodian Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff Provides onsite supervision of custodial crews as assigned; maintains an attractive, sanitary and safe facility for students, staff, and public. Communicates information in response to inquiries; ensures rooms are clean and ready for meetings, classroom activities, and events; maintains facilities to minimize facility deterioration and damage. Oversees the work activities of assigned site custodial personnel for the purpose of ensuring activities are completed within assigned time frames and in compliance with campus standards. Works under moderate supervision that relies on initiative and good judgment to be an effective leader. Read more LVN Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Nursing Staff The Licensed Vocational Nurse (LVN) provides nursing care and clinical support for patients in a healthcare setting. The LVN assists in the delivery of patient care for individuals who are ill, injured, or seeking preventive health services. Working under the supervision of a registered nurse, physician, or other licensed healthcare provider, the LVN performs clinical procedures, monitors patient conditions, and supports the healthcare team in implementing treatment plans. Read more LVN Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Nursing Staff HSC Health is seeking a compassionate LVN to join our dynamic team of healthcare providers at the University of North Texas Clinical Practice Group with the Center for Older Adults. This role requires a candidate with strong organizational skills, a wide set of interests and skill set, and strong interpersonal communication abilities. Candidate must have the ability to assess patients quickly and accurately. Exhibits compassion, understanding, the ability to work well in teams, and the ability to function in a fast-paced environment is critical for this position. Read more Director of Forensic Education Programs Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Advancement/Development HSC Health Staff The Director, Forensic Education Programs will be responsible for managing, organizing, developing, implementing, facilitating, administrating and evaluating all of CHI’s forensic training and educational programs for forensic scientists, law enforcement and medicolegal stakeholders. Among these will be The Texas Forensic Analyst Apprenticeship Pilot Program, created to supplement training for accredited forensic DNA laboratories throughout Texas. This position will be responsible for the development of training curriculum and supporting materials, the oversight of the program’s apprenticeships to ensure timely completion, and collaboration with subject matter experts and the state oversight agencies as needed to ensure delivery of a comprehensive training program with successful return. The position will also manage CHI’s existing training partnerships and expand its profile as a statewide, national, and international, center for forensic training, developing partnerships, tailoring programs, and utilizing CHI’s team of experts to meet the evolving needs of the forensic science community. Read more Donor Care Coordinator Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Administrative/Office Support Willed Body Program (UNT Health Only) Staff The Donor Care Coordinator will work closely with program staff, cremation providers, and donor families to ensure continuity, accuracy, and dignity throughout the donor's journey through the program. The position requires exceptional attention to detail, organizational skills, discretion, and the ability to approach human remains and donor materials with professionalism and respect. Read more Academic Program Coordinator Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff The Department of Public Health at TCOM is seeking to hire an Academic Program Coordinator who will provide instrumental support to the portfolio of the Associate Dean for Community Partnerships and Practice. Read more Program Project Coordinator Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff The Program Project Coordinator is a key member of the Faculty Success Office team and is expected to be a partner in providing career-track-relevant faculty development programming, support, and resource planning that supports UNT Health’s mission. The Program Project Coordinator works closely with the Executive Director of Faculty Success and other university unit leaders, including Faculty Senate committees to assess faculty success needs and provide relevant programming. The Program Project Coordinator’s primary focus is supporting the Executive Director of Faculty Success programs and initiatives. Read more Senior Program Manager Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff The Senior Program Manager position to provide research administrative support across the Texas Child Mental Health Care Consortium (TCMHCC) and Public Health (PH) research administration. The role will strengthen coordination across internal and external partners, improve oversight of research-related expenditures, and support timely, compliant execution of grant-funded and institutionally supported activities at TCMHCC and PH. Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Research Administration Research Support - Laboratory/Non-Laboratory Staff The Postdoctoral Research Associate's duties are related to research activities utilizing an advanced level of knowledge within their perspective field. They will also contribute to writing proposals and papers, while helping to maintain laboratory equipment, and may contribute to the training and supervision of students or any other assigned individuals. Read more Fire Safety Technician Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Construction Management Staff The Fire Safety Technician is responsible for the operation and maintenance of life safety systems, including but not limited to fire alarms, fire suppression systems, fire extinguishers, emergency generators and elevators. Manages construction and maintenance activities to ensure institutional procedures are followed and compliance is maintained relative to all applicable local, state and federal regulatory requirement Read more Forensic Technologist - Missing Persons Unit Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Data Science Staff Perform lab duties as part of the Missing Persons Unit, to include DNA extraction, quantification, amplification and loading of forensic samples onto analytical instruments for analysis to support criminal and civil investigations. Assist in performing daily maintenance and stocking of laboratories. Read more Custodian Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff The Facilities Department at the University of North Texas Health Science Center is seeking to hire a Custodian to join our team. Responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to:  Disinfecting, sanitizing and stocking rest rooms.  Cleaning office areas.  Vacuuming.  Trash removal.  Recycling removal.  Cleaning public area glass, windows, entrance doors, elevators.  Cleaning assigned laboratory. Read more Senior Compliance Officer (CLIA Laboratory Quality Manager) Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Compliance Staff This temporary role will support laboratory preparation and CLIA certification while overseeing quality control and quality assurance processes, regulatory compliance, operational readiness, and laboratory documentation and reporting. These responsibilities are critical to ensuring compliance with CLIA regulations and institutional standards while supporting the laboratory's successful implementation and ongoing operations. Read more Director of Award Management Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Advancement/Development Research Administration Staff The Director of Award Management provides operational leadership for the University's post-award research administration function, ensuring compliant and efficient administration of sponsored awards from award acceptance through closeout. This position oversees the daily operations of the Post-Award team while partnering closely with the Assistant Vice President of Sponsored Programs to implement strategic initiatives, improve business processes, and promote operational excellence across the Office of Sponsored Programs.\n    The Director serves as a subject matter expert in federal, state, institutional, and sponsor regulations governing sponsored programs and provides leadership in financial stewardship, compliance, risk management, and customer service. The position collaborates extensively with principal investigators, departmental administrators, Research Financial Services, Research Compliance, and institutional leadership to support the University's research mission. Read more Gastroenterologist Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems HSC Health Staff We are seeking a dedicated and skilled Gastroenterologist to join the UNT Health Clinical Practice Group. This position offers a unique opportunity to practice in an academic setting, engaging in a well-rounded blend of clinical care, and opportunities for teaching, and research.  The successful candidate will provide patient care in both the outpatient clinic and hospital settings, performing procedures and managing complex cases in the hospital. In addition to clinical responsibilities, you will contribute to the education and mentorship of health profession students, medical students, residents, and GI fellows. Read more Forensic Analyst - Missing Persons Unit Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Data Science Staff Responsibilities include conducting forensic DNA analysis on samples submitted to CHI for criminal and missing persons investigations to help establish the identity of the individual, maintaining accurate testing and quality control records, and providing legal testimony regarding the methods used and results obtained in the conducted forensic examinations. Read more Custodian Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff The Facilities Department at the University of North Texas Health Science Center is seeking to hire a Custodian to join our team. Responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to:     Disinfecting, sanitizing and stocking rest rooms.   Cleaning office areas.   Vacuuming.   Trash removal.   Recycling removal.   Cleaning public area glass, windows, entrance doors, elevators.   Cleaning assigned laboratory. Read more Enrollment Services Specialist Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff The Enrollment Services Specialist facilitates Admissions and Records/Registration issues for students and faculty. They will focus on problem-solving and assisting applicants in overcoming challenges during the admissions process. They will also be required to travel inside and outside Texas to recruitment fairs that attract students suitable for multiple UNT Health colleges and programs. Read more Title IX Coordinator Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Finance Human Resources Staff Serves as the UNT Health Fort Worth university official responsible for knowledge of Title IX regulations, OCR reporting requirements, and related federal compliance frameworks. responsible for developing, implementing, coordinating, and overseeing compliance with all aspects of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX), the Violence Against Women Reauthorization Act (VAWA) and Campus SaVe Act. Skilled in collecting, analyzing, and interpreting sensitive case data to produce accurate, timely compliance reports. Ability to maintain secure, detailed records and use data systems to monitor case progress, identify trends, and support institutional decision‑making. Proven capacity to translate complex data into clear, actionable insights for leadership while ensuring adherence to confidentiality and regulatory standards. Responsible for monitoring the ongoing publication of the university’s related regulations and policies, compliant investigation of complaints and overall activities for compliance with Title IX requirements; and assuring dissemination of the grievance procedure.\n\nWhile this position is hybrid, the majority of the work week will be present on-campus.  The schedule is dependent on programming, events, training, etc., and will fluctuate as needed. Read more Institutional Review Board Compliance Manager Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Compliance Staff The Office of Research Compliance (ORC) at the University of North Texas Health Science Center, in conjunction with the North Texas Regional Institutional Review Board (NTR IRB), is seeking to hire an IRB Compliance Manager to join our team. This position will report directly to the Director of the NTR IRB and will also work closely with the ORC. Responsibilities include (but are not limited to) the following: 1) Assist with development and implementation of human research protection for all NTR IRB partners; 2) Perform comprehensive administrative and regulatory reviews of designated IRB submissions (which include biomedical, clinical trial, and social/behavioral science studies) by ensuring applications/submissions meet all federal agency regulatory requirements for human subject research; 3) Assist with ongoing education and training for all affiliated researchers to ensure appropriate compliance with federal, state and university/institutional policies and regulations associated with human subject research; 4) Prepare documents for review by the IRB reviewers/committee; 5) Assist with oversight, attendance and coordination of IRB committee meetings and communicate outcomes to investigators, relevant institutional officials, and federal agencies (when needed); 6) Assist with development and roll out of inhouse compliance training programs, workshops, seminars, guidance documents and other outreach and educational tools and training related to IRB and human subject research; 7) Assist in the daily activities, accreditation efforts, special projects and operation of the NTR IRB. Read more Quality Assurance (QA) Analyst Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Compliance Staff The Quality Assurance Analyst is part of the Quality Management team, led by the Quality Director (QD). This position will assist the Director and Assistant Quality Director (AQD) in ensuring the highest level of quality assurance and quality control for CHI’s labs, by supporting their efforts to manage and implement the requirements of the accreditation programs and standard practices for the Center. Read more Plumber Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Construction Management Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff Plumbing repair work and plumbing installation work in commercial buildings on college campus; including work on laboratories, bathrooms, and building infrastructure. Read more Manager, Clinical Nurse Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Nursing Staff The Clinical Nurse Manager will work in partnership with the Clinic Managers and Medical Directors to administer and coordinate all clinical and nursing obligations within UNT Health Clinical Practice Group locations. Read more Maintenance Technician Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Construction Management Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff The Maintenance Technician completes work in a manner that will retain or improve customer satisfaction and the quality of the surrounding area. Some of the work performed includes the following: office and laboratory moves, delivery of large items, event set ups, maintenance and repair of event furniture and driving a shuttle bus. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 31 in total ‹ 1 2 › 3500 Camp Bowie Blvd. Fort Worth, Texas 76107 Phone: 855.878.7650 (option #2) HRemployment@untsystem.edu Quick Links Home View All System Jobs My Settings Applicant Login Equal Employment Opportunity | Notice of Nondiscrimination | Title IX | Workplace Posters Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
