esident of Financial Planning, Analysis, Strategy The Associate Vice President of Financial Planning, Analysis Strategy (AVP) is a fulltime administrative position that serves as the primary support and advisor to the Chief Financial Officer (CFO) in all finance and administrative matters, resource allocation, and in University strategy development, execution, and evaluation. The AVP oversees the Budget Office, Sponsored Projects, Accounting Reporting, Student Business Services, Property Management, and Central Receiving. Dallas, Texas, United States DAL-Budget & Finance Executive Administration Staff Read more Board Professional and Office Manager The Board Professional and Office Manager is a full-time professional support position for the Foundation’s President and Chief Executive Officer (CEO), the UNT Foundation office, and the Foundation Board of Directors.  This full-time, professional staff provides specialized administrative, organizational and communication support on a daily basis.  This person works closely with other Foundation and University staff and with the Board of Directors of the Foundation and reports directly to the CEO. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Advancement Advancement/Development Staff Read more Assistant Professor of Semiconductors The Department of Physics invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor. The candidate's research should be in the area of Semiconductors (experimental). Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Science Faculty Read more Assistant/Associate Professor of Biophysics The Department of Physics at the University of North Texas (UNT) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level. The candidate's research should be in the area of Biophysics (experimental). Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Science Faculty Read more Associate/Assistant Professor of Cancer Biology The Department of Biological Sciences at the University of North Texas invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the area of Cancer Biology. Preference will be given to applicants with research interests in the areas of physiology and molecular biology of cancer, or development and application of immunotherapy methods for cancer treatment. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Science Faculty Read more Transportation Attendant Parking & Transport Attendant within the University of North Texas Parking and Transportation Services department supports campus mobility, parking rules enforcement, and safe transit operations. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-VP Finance & Admin Police Department/Public Safety Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Non-Student Work Control Assistant - Part Time This position is responsible for functioning as a contact between Facilities and its customers, and for assisting other employees in managing work orders for the campus. This position operates the computerized Maintenance Management System (WebTMA) daily to receive and process service requests from UNT customers. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-VP Finance & Admin Administrative/Office Support Hourly Read more Non-Student Hourly Booth Attendant The Booth Attendant serves as a primary point of contact for individuals visiting the University of North Texas (UNT) and plays an important role as an ambassador for the university. This position provides exceptional customer service to students, faculty, staff, visitors, parents, university officials, and community members while assisting with parking-related needs and questions. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-VP Finance & Admin Police Department/Public Safety Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Hourly Upward Bound Saturday Reading teacher UNT Upward Bound is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic READING teacher to provide reading and literacy instruction to high school students during our Saturday academic sessions. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Administrative Coordinator This position provides administrative support to the department chair and academic department of over 20 regular faculty plus doctoral students and adjuncts. Major duties include scheduling the department's semester class schedule through careful coordination with the faculty and chair; managing departmental budgets and faculty expenses, processing salaried and hourly payroll; facilitating employee onboarding and off boarding processes, procuring goods/services via purchasing card and requisitions; securing classrooms and transmitting changes to Registrar; facilitating faculty and staff recruitment by managing postings and applicants, scheduling video and campus interviews, arranging travel; and supporting student organization events. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Adjunct Instructor - Counseling and Human Services - Spring 2027 UNT Dallas is bridging the gap between education and workforce readiness through our innovative Classroom to Career initiative. This initiative integrates experiential learning—such as internships, service learning, and project-based collaborations with industry partners—into every student’s academic journey. By emphasizing high-impact practices,\n\nUNT Dallas is seeking qualified individuals to establish a robust pool of talented adjunct instructors for our growing counseling programs. Selected candidates will be responsible for teaching master's-level counseling courses across multiple formats including face-to-face, hybrid, and online instruction using Canvas learning management system. The ideal candidates will demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching excellence and dedication to student success.\n\nBeginning Spring 2026 semester, teaching opportunities will be available in Group Counseling, Family Counseling, Substance Abuse Treatment, Professional School Counseling, Practicum in School Counseling, and Career Counseling. Candidates will be drawn from this talent pool as positions become available. As our programs continue to expand, additional teaching opportunities may arise across our counseling curriculum. Dallas, Texas, United States DAL-Academic Aff & Stdnt Success Faculty - Human Services Adjunct Read more Senior Student Services Coordinator This position serves as a high level case management position for both Care Team and Student Conduct. As it specifically relates to student conduct, this position is responsible for the investigation and adjudication of student conduct cases, which includes high level decision making such as assigning suspensions and expulsions. Additionally, this position maintains on-call responsibilities for responding to student emergencies. Finally, this position assists in prevention and education programming responsibilities related to Care Team and Conduct topics. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - Skellam Lab The Skellam lab at the University of North Texas is seeking a highly motivated and determined Postdoctoral Research Associate with experience in the isolation and structural elucidation of natural products from complex crude extracts. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff Read more Student Finance Service Specialist This position is responsible for accurately processing student finance transactions and processes daily cash receipts for the institution. This includes maintaining accounting records and preparation of financial reports. Work in collaboration with other administrative departments. Provide guidance regarding student and department accounts. Delivers exceptional customer service to students and their parent. Conduct research and provide reports related to reconciliation issues. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Finance Financial Aid Staff Read more Systems Integration Architect This position is responsible for ownership of day today technical management including the designing, procuring, installing and maintaining of all components (digital, communications and other) in setting up large, complex buildings and rooms within the university. This position ensures the system and component specific choices meet the scalability and operational effectiveness needs of UNT. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Information Technology Staff Read more Senior Systems Integration Architect This position would support the purpose of solidifying the function of Integrated Systems and Development and Operations for UNT (DevOps). This job includes exercising a working knowledge of Development and Operations best practices for a team that utilizes tools such as application development (multi platform), web development, coding as infrastructure, SQL server and database bound applications, automation as operations. The primary focus of this manager will be Development. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Information Technology Staff Read more Cross Functional IT Support Coordinator This position provides high level technical support for Faculty, Staff, Students, and Guests of UNT. Duties include maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing A/V systems, digital signage systems, student/lab computers; responding to user requests for technology assistance, training, and support; providing technology support for campus events; assisting with other departmental services such as checking out equipment, installing software, responding to tickets, etc. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Administrative/Office Support Information Technology Staff Read more Evening Facility Coordinator This position is responsible for assisting with the planning, conducting, managing, staffing and equipping of 