ed and reported. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Budget Officer This position provides budgetary, financial, and analytical support to the UNT System Information Technology organization. The position assists in the development, monitoring, and forecasting of operating and capital budgets; prepares financial analyses and reports; and supports strategic decision-making by the Chief Information Officer and IT leadership team. The position reports to the Senior Director of IT Finance and Vendor Management and serves as a key resource for financial planning, budget management, and technology investment analysis. Denton, Texas, United States SYS-Information Technology Accounting/Finance/Budget/Payroll Information Technology Staff Read more Hourly Writer, Editor & Research Specialist This position is to support the development of written works for communications and reporting within the Division of Student Affairs and externally to stakeholders and counterparts in the field. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Hourly Read more Sr Grant & Contract Acct Anlst The Sr Grants & Contracts Accounting Analyst position in the Grants & Contracts Administration unit (Post-Award team) is responsible for administering highly complex research grant awards and budgets to maintain fiscal compliance and to minimize University liability and legal/financial risk campus-wide. The position reviews and sets up highly complex awards, monitors them, prepares invoices, financial reports and performs the award close-out. Prepares documents for requests for information and audits. Interpret sponsor guidelines/stay abreast of federal/state policy changes for 100+ external sponsors with varying legal/financial requirements. Vital campus expert, mitigate risk campus-wide in high-risk areas. Develop/deliver complex campus-wide training, develop and implement internal reporting and analysis tools. Develop policies/internal controls. Manage special projects. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Research & Innovation Administrative/Office Support Research Administration Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - The Horn Lab within the Department of Biological Sciences and BioDiscovery Institute (BDI). The Horn Laboratory in The BioDiscovery Institute and Department of Biological Sciences at the University of North Texas is seeking to hire a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to join our team. Our lab broadly focuses on characterizing molecular processes and engineering lipid-based bioproducts in plant systems Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff Read more Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations The College of Visual Arts and Design (CVAD) at the University of North Texas (UNT) is seeking a Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations to provide strategic leadership for college-level marketing, communications, and public relations. The Director develops and implements an integrated communications strategy that advances the college’s priorities, strengthens its visibility and reputation, and supports student recruitment, engagement, advancement, and community outreach.\nThe Director oversees CVAD communications across multiple platforms and formats, including the college website, social media, newsletters, press releases, advertising, donor and recruitment materials, publications, short-form video, and other print and digital content. The position creates and edits clear, compelling, and audience-focused communications and identifies opportunities to share the accomplishments and impact of CVAD students, faculty, staff, alumni, programs, and partners.\nWorking closely with UNT’s University Brand Strategy and Communications (UBSC), the Director ensures that CVAD communications align with university branding, communication standards, institutional priorities, and applicable policies. The position requires exceptional writing, editing, proofreading, project-management, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines.\nThe Director is responsible for ensuring that web, digital, print, and multimedia communications meet institutional policies and accessibility requirements, including ADA compliance. Additional responsibilities include cultivating media and campus relationships, researching marketing opportunities and best practices, supporting major college events and initiatives, and supervising student employees. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Advertising/Marketing Staff Read more Student Media Coordinator It is responsible for supporting multiple student media groups, including the Debate Team, Comm Future Pros, DCTV, Hatch, KNTU, NT Daily, NTTV, and Swoop. This position will perform or assist with a variety of administrative including (1) payroll processes; (2) purchases for student meetings and events; (3) requisition and invoice management; (4) reserve rooms for student media meetings; (5) working with faculty advisors and staff managers of various student media areas; (6) other duties as may be assigned. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Digital Accessibility Specialist The Digital Accessibility Specialist within the Office of Disability Access is a student-, faculty-, and staff-facing position focused on advancing digital accessibility across the University of North Texas. The Digital Accessibility Specialist works directly with students with disabilities and faculty to identify, troubleshoot, and resolve digital accessibility barriers that may impact a student’s access to course materials, instructional technologies, or participation in the academic experience. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support St