nally, this position maintains on-call responsibilities for responding to student emergencies. Finally, this position assists in prevention and education programming responsibilities related to Care Team and Conduct topics. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Student Finance Service Specialist This position is responsible for accurately processing student finance transactions and processes daily cash receipts for the institution. This includes maintaining accounting records and preparation of financial reports. Work in collaboration with other administrative departments. Provide guidance regarding student and department accounts. Delivers exceptional customer service to students and their parent. Conduct research and provide reports related to reconciliation issues. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Finance Financial Aid Staff Read more Financial Aid Counselor Evaluates and analyzes financial information submitted by applicants to determine eligibility for financial assistance and determines type and amount of aid to be awarded in accordance with established federal and university standards and guidelines. Coordinates and administers assigned financial aid programs such as the federal work study program, Pell/SEOG, and state grants. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Financial Aid Staff Read more Adjunct Assistant Professor This position supports the Physician Assistant Studies Program through a combination of teaching, student assessment, admissions participation, and departmental service. The faculty member will assist course directors in delivering high-quality didactic and clinical instruction, evaluating student performance, and grading assignments, examinations, and clinical activities. \n\nResponsibilities include teaching and demonstrating clinical skills in classroom, laboratory, and clinical learning environments; delivering lectures and facilitating learning activities as assigned; and providing educational support across multiple courses within the curriculum. The individual will also contribute to student recruitment efforts by participating in applicant interviews and admissions selection processes. In addition, the faculty member will collaborate with program leadership and fellow faculty on a variety of departmental initiatives, accreditation-related activities, committee work, and other program responsibilities as needed. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to student success, academic excellence, and the continued growth and development of the Physician Assistant Studies Program. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Texas College of Osteopathic Medicine Faculty Read more Student Services Coordinator (Center for Academic Performance) The Writing Coordinator in the Center for Academic Performance is a hybrid position, working both on campus and remotely to aid in the support of students by providing academic writing and presentation support. This position will meet individually with students, both in person and via online meeting platforms, to assess and provide feedback regarding writing skills. They will work closely with other departments and academic programs to integrate writing skills with curriculum. They will provide students with presentations and workshops focused on the enhancement of writing skills. When on campus, the Writing Coordinator does work out of a shared office space, with access to space to meet privately with students. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Assistant Professor and Director of Academic Education The Department of Physician Assistant Studies is seeking a PA educator for an open rank faculty position with an administrative appointment as Director of Academic Education (DAE). The ideal candidate will be a collaborative team player with excellent written and verbal communication skills, experience in teaching and scholarship, and proficiency with common software applications. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering instruction, assessing student performance, participating in program evaluation and student recruitment activities, mentoring students in their professional development, conducting research related to PA practice or education, pursuing grant opportunities, and engaging in other scholarly activities. Faculty are given release time to maintain clinical skills through clinical practice opportunities and enjoy a collaborative academic environment, competitive benefits, and opportunities for professional growth.\n\nIn addition to a PA Faculty role, the Director of Academic Education (DAE) collaborates closely with the Program Director, Curriculum Committee, Student Performance Committee, Communication Committee, and Accreditation Committee to oversee and maintain curricular coherence. The DAE secures adequate classroom and laboratory space and scheduling, ensures curricular alignment with ARC-PA accreditation standards and the overall mission of the program, and facilitates cross department communication while acting as a liaison between departments on campus to coordinate education and testing for PA Students. The DAE works with course directors and the Director of Clinical Education to design, implement, coordinate, schedule, and evaluate educational activities taking place in the didactic and clinical phase of the curriculum. The DAE is directly responsible for the scheduling of the semester orientation meetings, didactic courses, course sequencing, and evaluating student performance. The DAE provides oversight and direction to course directors on course content, methods used to deliver course content, instructional faculty, student assessment, and evaluation of student assessments. Major changes are coordinated between the DAE, PAS-CC, and the PD. The DAE is responsible for ensuring that didactic courses are evaluated by course directors at the end of each semester and tracks the effectiveness of changes made to those courses. This position may be assigned additional duties and may be required to participate in special projects, consistent with the responsibilities and objectives of the position and the needs of the department, college, and university. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Texas College of Osteopathic Medicine Faculty Read more Medical Assistant UNT Health Family Medicine is seeking a compassionate Medical Assistant to join our dynamic team of healthcare providers at the University of North Texas Health Science Center. This role requires a candidate with strong organizational skills, a wide set of interests and skill set, and strong interpersonal communication abilities. Candidate must exhibit compassion, understanding, the ability to work well in teams, and the ability to function in a fastpaced environment is critical for this position. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Medical Assistants Staff Read more Academic Program Manager This Academic Program Manager is responsible for the academic administration, coordination, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of TCOM’s four-year Professional Identity and Health Systems Practice (PIHSP) curriculum. PIHSP is a longitudinal curriculum integrating professional identity formation with Health Systems Science and related competencies across Years 1–4 of medical school. The Academic Program Manager serves as a central operational resource for the Director of PIHSP Course, Director of Health Systems Science, Innovation and Leadership, Chair of Medical Education and Health Systems Science, PISHP course and section directors, PIHSP senior academic program manager, faculty, staff, students, and curriculum leadership.\n\nThe Academic Program Manager coordinates PIHSP components including Ethics, Health Systems Science, Innovation, Patient Safety, Population and Public Health, Interprofessional Education, Health Promotion and Disease Prevention, Health Policy, Health Informatics and Artificial Intelligence, Emotional Intelligence, leadership, and other current and evolving PIHSP content. The employee ensures alignment of activities, objectives, assessments, student experiences, faculty responsibilities, and curricular documentation across all four years. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Assistant Professor and Director of Clinical Education The Department of Physician Assistant Studies is seeking a PA educator for an open rank faculty position with an administrative appointment as Director of Clinical Education. The ideal candidate will be a collaborative team player with excellent written and verbal communication skills, experience in teaching and scholarship, and proficiency with common software applications. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering instruction, assessing student performance, participating in program evaluation and student recruitment activities, mentoring students in their professional development, conducting research related to PA practice or education, pursuing grant opportunities, and engaging in other scholarly activities. Faculty are given release time to maintain clinical skills through clinical practice opportunities and enjoy a collaborative academic environment, competitive benefits, and opportunities for professional growth.\n\nIn addition to a PA Faculty role, the Director of Clinical Education (DCE) serves as a member of the Department of PA Studies leadership team. The role oversees the clinical phase of the program, ensuring curricular alignment with ARC-PA accreditation standards and the overall mission of the program. This position integrates strategic oversight of clinical curriculum, site management, faculty coordination, and external clinical partnership development to support high-quality clinical education and student success.\n\nThe DCE collaborates closely with the Program Director, Director of Academic Education, Associate Program Director, Executive Committee, Curriculum Committee, Communication Committee, Senior Project Coordinator, and Clinical Site Coordinator to maintain curricular coherence, ensure an adequate number and diversity of clinical sites for student education, and facilitate effective communication across all clinical education activities. The DCE will work closely with the DAE to implement, coordinate, schedule and evaluate educational activities taking place in the clinical phase of the curriculum. The\n\nDCE will also cultivate and sustain external clinical relationships with healthcare organizations, providers, and community partners, leveraging these partnerships to enhance clinical training opportunities, expand clinical placement capacity, and strengthen connections between the program and the healthcare community. This position may be assigned additional duties and may be required to participate in special projects, consistent with the responsibilities and objectives of the position and the needs of the department, college, and university. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Texas College of Osteopathic Medicine Faculty Read more Senior Custodian Provides onsite supervision of custodial crews as assigned; maintains an attractive, sanitary and safe facility for students, staff, and public. Communicates information in response to inquiries; ensures rooms are clean and ready for meetings, classroom activities, and events; maintains facilities to minimize facility deterioration and damage. Oversees the work activities of assigned site custodial personnel for the purpose of ensuring activities are completed within assigned time frames and in compliance with campus standards. Works under moderate supervision that relies on initiative and good judgment to be an effective leader. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff Read more LVN The Licensed Vocational Nurse (LVN) provides nursing care and clinical support for patients in a healthcare setting. The LVN assists in the delivery of patient care for individuals who are ill, injured, or seeking preventive health services. Working under the supervision of a registered nurse, physician, or other licensed healthcare provider, the LVN performs clinical procedures, monitors patient conditions, and supports the healthcare team in implementing treatment plans. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Nursing Staff Read more LVN HSC Health is seeking a compassionate LVN to join our dynamic team of healthcare providers at the University of North Texas Clinical Practice Group with the Center for Older Adults. This role requires a candidate with strong organizational skills, a wide set of interests and skill set, and strong interpersonal communication abilities. Candidate must have the ability to assess patients quickly and accurately. Exhibits compassion, understanding, the ability to work well in teams, and the ability to function in a fast-paced environment is critical for this position. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Nursing Staff Read more Director of Forensic Education Programs The Director, Forensic Education Programs will be responsible for managing, organizing, developing, implementing, facilitating, administrating and evaluating all of CHI’s forensic training and educational programs for forensic scientists, law enforcement and medicolegal stakeholders. Among these will be The Texas Forensic Analyst Apprenticeship Pilot Program, created to supplement training for accredited forensic DNA laboratories throughout Texas. This position will be responsible for the development of training curriculum and supporting materials, the oversight of the program’s apprenticeships to ensure timely completion, and collaboration with subject matter experts and the state oversight agencies as needed to ensure delivery of a comprehensive training program with successful return. The position will also manage CHI’s existing training partnerships and expand its profile as a statewide, national, and international, center for forensic training, developing partnerships, tailoring programs, and utilizing CHI’s team of experts to meet the evolving needs of the forensic science community. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Advancement/Development HSC Health Staff Read more Donor Care Coordinator The Donor Care Coordinator will work closely with program staff, cremation providers, and donor families to ensure continuity, accuracy, and dignity throughout the donor's journey through the program. The position requires exceptional attention to detail, organizational skills, discretion, and the ability to approach human remains and donor materials with professionalism and respect. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Administrative/Office Support Willed Body Program (UNT Health Only) Staff Read more Academic Program Coordinator The Department of Public Health at TCOM is seeking to hire an Academic Program Coordinator who will provide instrumental support to the portfolio of the Associate Dean for Community Partnerships and Practice. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Program Project Coordinator The Program Project Coordinator is a key member of the Faculty Success Office team and is expected to be a partner in providing career-track-relevant faculty development programming, support, and resource planning that supports UNT Health’s mission. The Program Project Coordinator works closely with the Executive Director of Faculty Success and other university unit leaders, including Faculty Senate committees to assess faculty success needs and provide relevant programming. The Program Project Coordinator’s primary focus is supporting the Executive Director of Faculty Success programs and initiatives. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Part-Time Proctor and Administrative Support This position is part of the Division of Student Affairs at UNT Health Fort Worth and the Office of Disability Access (ODA). This position supports UNT Health students and academic departments with a wide variety of student assessment (examination/testing) activities for students registered with the ODA and receiving disability-related accommodations. This position fosters student success by ensuring that student knowledge is effectively measured, approved accommodations are provided, and academic curricular goals are achieved. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Hourly Read more Patient Access Representative The Patient Access Representative is primarily responsible for greeting patients, managing appointment scheduling, answering phone calls, handling patient check-in/check-out procedures, collecting payments, maintaining patient records, and ensuring a positive patient experience. This position serves as the first point of contact for our patients. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems Administrative/Office Support Hourly Read more HR Business Partner/Senior HR Business Partner The Human Resources Department at the University of North Texas System is seeking to hire a Human Resources Business Partner to join our team. This role serves as a strategic HR partner, fostering strong relationships across departments to support employee engagement, retention, and organizational effectiveness. It leverages HR data to inform decision-making, ensures policy compliance, and guides departments through change management and process improvements. The position also supports professional development, compensation and classification strategies, and contributes to HR program enhancements. Through cross-functional collaboration and independent project management, it ensures seamless HR service delivery aligned with university goals. Fort Worth, Texas, United States SYS-Human Resources Human Resources Staff Read more Senior Program Manager The Senior Program Manager position to provide research administrative support across the Texas Child Mental Health Care Consortium (TCMHCC) and Public Health (PH) research administration. The role will strengthen coordination across internal and external partners, improve oversight of research-related expenditures, and support timely, compliant execution of grant-funded and institutionally supported activities at TCMHCC and PH. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate The Postdoctoral Research Associate's duties are related to research activities utilizing an advanced level of knowledge within their perspective field. They will also contribute to writing proposals and papers, while helping to maintain laboratory equipment, and may contribute to the training and supervision of students or any other assigned individuals. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Research Administration Research Support - Laboratory/Non-Laboratory Staff Read more Fire Safety Technician The Fire Safety Technician is responsible for the operation and maintenance of life safety systems, including but not limited to fire alarms, fire suppression systems, fire extinguishers, emergency generators and elevators. Manages construction and maintenance activities to ensure institutional procedures are followed and compliance is maintained relative to all applicable local, state and federal regulatory requirement Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Construction Management Staff Read more Assistant Professor - Clinical Nutrition The Department of Personalized Health and Well-Being, College of Health Professions, is seeking an experienced Registered Dietitian for a full-time, 12-month faculty position to teach in the Master of Science in Clinical Nutrition Coordinated Program (MSCN). The MSCN program prepares students to become Registered Dietitian Nutritionists. This position may be hybrid, combining remote and in-person responsibilities at the UNT Health Fort Worth campus. The faculty member will engage in innovative teaching, student mentorship, course and curriculum development, and continuous quality improvement. Additional responsibilities include, but are not limited to, contributing to the ACEND accreditation process, collaborating on research, and participating in service across the department, college, and university. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Pharmacy Faculty Read more Assistant Professor The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of North Texas Health Science Center at Fort Worth invites applications for a full-time, 12-month faculty position at the Assistant Professor rank in the residential Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) program, effective immediately. The primary focus of this position will be to contribute to the department’s teaching mission while supporting research within the residential DPT curriculum.\n\nResponsibilities include teaching in the entry level program, maintaining or collaborating on an active program of scholarship, contributing collegially to departmental research initiatives, and mentoring DPT students in scholarly activities. The faculty member will contribute to teaching in the entry-level DPT curriculum in areas consistent with their expertise. Additional responsibilities include advising students, participating in departmental and university service, and collaborating with faculty to support program operations and accreditation requirements.\n\nThe successful candidate will contribute to the department’s commitment to advancing evidence-informed practice, fostering student engagement in research and scholarship, and supporting the mission of the department to develop innovative solutions for a healthier community. The faculty member will also engage in interprofessional education and collaboration with faculty across the university, school, and program. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Pharmacy Faculty Read more Forensic Technologist - Missing Persons Unit Perform lab duties as part of the Missing Persons Unit, to include DNA extraction, quantification, amplification and loading of forensic samples onto analytical instruments for analysis to support criminal and civil investigations. Assist in performing daily maintenance and stocking of laboratories. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Data Science Staff Read more Custodian The Facilities Department at the University of North Texas Health Science Center is seeking to hire a Custodian to join our team. Responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to:  Disinfecting, sanitizing and stocking rest rooms.  Cleaning office areas.  Vacuuming.  Trash removal.  Recycling removal.  Cleaning public area glass, windows, entrance doors, elevators.  Cleaning assigned laboratory. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Operations & Business Mgmt Facilities/Maintenance/Custodial Staff Read more Senior Compliance Officer (CLIA Laboratory Quality Manager) This temporary role will support laboratory preparation and CLIA certification while overseeing quality control and quality assurance processes, regulatory compliance, operational readiness, and laboratory documentation and reporting. These responsibilities are critical to ensuring compliance with CLIA regulations and institutional standards while supporting the laboratory's successful implementation and ongoing operations. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Compliance Staff Read more Director of Award Management The Director of Award Management provides operational leadership for the University's post-award research administration function, ensuring compliant and efficient administration of sponsored awards from award acceptance through closeout. This position oversees the daily operations of the Post-Award team while partnering closely with the Assistant Vice President of Sponsored Programs to implement strategic initiatives, improve business processes, and promote operational excellence across the Office of Sponsored Programs.\n    The Director serves as a subject matter expert in federal, state, institutional, and sponsor regulations governing sponsored programs and provides leadership in financial stewardship, compliance, risk management, and customer service. The position collaborates extensively with principal investigators, departmental administrators, Research Financial Services, Research Compliance, and institutional leadership to support the University's research mission. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Div of Rsrch & Innovation Advancement/Development Research Administration Staff Read more Gastroenterologist We are seeking a dedicated and skilled Gastroenterologist to join the UNT Health Clinical Practice Group. This position offers a unique opportunity to practice in an academic setting, engaging in a well-rounded blend of clinical care, and opportunities for teaching, and research.  The successful candidate will provide patient care in both the outpatient clinic and hospital settings, performing procedures and managing complex cases in the hospital. In addition to clinical responsibilities, you will contribute to the education and mentorship of health profession students, medical students, residents, and GI fellows. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Health Systems HSC Health Staff Read more Assistant Professor - Office of Rural Medical Education The Family Medicine Department at the University of North Texas Health Science Center is seeking a part time Assistant/Associate Professor faculty member in the Office of Rural Medical Education (ORME) to teach and mentor Doctor of Osteopathy medical students for the Rural Osteopathic Medical Education (ROME) programs. Responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to:\n\n· Assist with the planning and facilitating of ROME Courses, ROME events, and other ROME programming Participation as faculty through a combination of classroom instruction, clinical instruction, and Rural field trips.\n\n· Participation as faculty through a combination of classroom instruction, clinical instruction, and Rural field trips. Fort Worth, Texas, United States HSC-Provost & Exec VP Faculty - Texas College of Osteopathic Medicine Faculty Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 59 in total ‹ 1 2 › 1901 Main St, Dallas, Tx 75201 Phone: 855.878.7650 (option #2) HRemployment@untsystem.edu Quick Links Home View All System Jobs My Settings Applicant Login Equal Employment Opportunity | Notice of Nondiscrimination | Title IX | Workplace Posters Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
