ogy of cancer, or development and application of immunotherapy methods for cancer treatment. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Science Faculty Read more Lecturer of Political Science and International Studies The faculty member will be expected to teach INST 2100 and advanced courses in political science and international studies, including courses in international security, national security, and area studies. with a preference for East Asian countries. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Liberal Arts/Social Sciences Faculty Read more Associate Clinical Professor: Electrical Engineering The Department of Electrical Engineering seeks qualified individuals for its clinical associate professor. The position is expected to teach courses in both undergraduate and graduate level in electrical engineering. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Engineering Faculty Read more Lecturer of Health Informatics and Health Librarianship The Department of Information Science invites applications for a lecturer position in Health Informatics and Health Librarianship. We are seeking excellent candidates with a background in current or emerging areas of health informatics and health librarianship, especially with a focus on artificial intelligence. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Faculty - Information Sciences Faculty - Libraries Faculty Read more Displaying all 7 entries 1155 Union Circle #311277, Denton, Tx 76203-5017 Phone: 855.878.7650 (option #2) HRemployment@untsystem.edu Quick Links Home View All System Jobs My Settings Applicant Login Equal Employment Opportunity | Notice of Nondiscrimination | Title IX | Workplace Posters Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experienc