ds and questions. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-VP Finance & Admin Police Department/Public Safety Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Hourly Upward Bound Saturday Reading teacher UNT Upward Bound is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic READING teacher to provide reading and literacy instruction to high school students during our Saturday academic sessions. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Administrative Coordinator This position provides administrative support to the department chair and academic department of over 20 regular faculty plus doctoral students and adjuncts. Major duties include scheduling the department's semester class schedule through careful coordination with the faculty and chair; managing departmental budgets and faculty expenses, processing salaried and hourly payroll; facilitating employee onboarding and off boarding processes, procuring goods/services via purchasing card and requisitions; securing classrooms and transmitting changes to Registrar; facilitating faculty and staff recruitment by managing postings and applicants, scheduling video and campus interviews, arranging travel; and supporting student organization events. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - Skellam Lab The Skellam lab at the University of North Texas is seeking a highly motivated and determined Postdoctoral Research Associate with experience in the isolation and structural elucidation of natural products from complex crude extracts. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff Read more Systems Integration Architect This position is responsible for ownership of day today technical management including the designing, procuring, installing and maintaining of all components (digital, communications and other) in setting up large, complex buildings and rooms within the university. This position ensures the system and component specific choices meet the scalability and operational effectiveness needs of UNT. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Information Technology Staff Read more Senior Systems Integration Architect This position would support the purpose of solidifying the function of Integrated Systems and Development and Operations for UNT (DevOps). This job includes exercising a working knowledge of Development and Operations best practices for a team that utilizes tools such as application development (multi platform), web development, coding as infrastructure, SQL server and database bound applications, automation as operations. The primary focus of this manager will be Development. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Information Technology Staff Read more Cross Functional IT Support Coordinator This position provides high level technical support for Faculty, Staff, Students, and Guests of UNT. Duties include maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing A/V systems, digital signage systems, student/lab computers; responding to user requests for technology assistance, training, and support; providing technology support for campus events; assisting with other departmental services such as checking out equipment, installing software, responding to tickets, etc. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Information Technology Administrative/Office Support Information Technology Staff Read more Evening Facility Coordinator This position is responsible for assisting with the planning, conducting, managing, staffing and equipping of the Informal Recreation program within Recreational Sports. Additionally, this position supervises the evening operations in the Pohl Recreation Center and other auxiliary facilities. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Internship Specialist The Career Center Department at the University of North Texas is seeking to hire an Internship Coordinator to join our team. Position is responsible for organizing and managing internship programs and events for assigned colleges; provide internship programming to students interested in working as an intern, and work with faculty and staff in the colleges to provide support for their internship programs within their colleges; work with academic counselors on internship procedures, ensure that student internships are meeting departmental requirements and receiving credit for their internship; work with Internship Team to grow and expand Career Treks Job Shadowing program, work with students through classes, student organizations and individually to promote the services as they seek to make internship decisions; reach out to companies that recruit students from their assigned colleges and strengthen/start a recruiting relationship with companies; ensure that all activities of the office are assessed and reported. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Sr Grant & Contract Acct Anlst The Sr Grants & Contracts Accounting Analyst position in the Grants & Contracts Administration unit (Post-Award team) is responsible for administering highly complex research grant awards and budgets to maintain fiscal compliance and to minimize University liability and legal/financial risk campus-wide. The position reviews and sets up highly complex awards, monitors them, prepares invoices, financial reports and performs the award close-out. Prepares documents for requests for information and audits. Interpret sponsor guidelines/stay abreast of federal/state policy changes for 100+ external sponsors with varying legal/financial requirements. Vital campus expert, mitigate risk campus-wide in high-risk areas. Develop/deliver complex campus-wide training, develop and implement internal reporting and analysis tools. Develop policies/internal controls. Manage special projects. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Research & Innovation Administrative/Office Support Research Administration Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - The Horn Lab within the Department of Biological Sciences and BioDiscovery Institute (BDI). The Horn Laboratory in The BioDiscovery Institute and Department of Biological Sciences at the University of North Texas is seeking to hire a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to join our team. Our lab broadly focuses on characterizing molecular processes and engineering lipid-based bioproducts in plant systems Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff Read more Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations The College of Visual Arts and Design (CVAD) at the University of North Texas (UNT) is seeking a Director of Communications, Marketing and Public Relations to provide strategic leadership for college-level marketing, communications, and public relations. The Director develops and implements an integrated communications strategy that advances the college’s priorities, strengthens its visibility and reputation, and supports student recruitment, engagement, advancement, and community outreach.\nThe Director oversees CVAD communications across multiple platforms and formats, including the college website, social media, newsletters, press releases, advertising, donor and recruitment materials, publications, short-form video, and other print and digital content. The position creates and edits clear, compelling, and audience-focused communications and identifies opportunities to share the accomplishments and impact of CVAD students, faculty, staff, alumni, programs, and partners.\nWorking closely with UNT’s University Brand Strategy and Communications (UBSC), the Director ensures that CVAD communications align with university branding, communication standards, institutional priorities, and applicable policies. The position requires exceptional writing, editing, proofreading, project-management, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines.\nThe Director is responsible for ensuring that web, digital, print, and multimedia communications meet institutional policies and accessibility requirements, including ADA compliance. Additional responsibilities include cultivating media and campus relationships, researching marketing opportunities and best practices, supporting major college events and initiatives, and supervising student employees. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Advertising/Marketing Staff Read more Student Media Coordinator It is responsible for supporting multiple student media groups, including the Debate Team, Comm Future Pros, DCTV, Hatch, KNTU, NT Daily, NTTV, and Swoop. This position will perform or assist with a variety of administrative including (1) payroll processes; (2) purchases for student meetings and events; (3) requisition and invoice management; (4) reserve rooms for student media meetings; (5) working with faculty advisors and staff managers of various student media areas; (6) other duties as may be assigned. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Digital Accessibility Specialist The Digital Accessibility Specialist within the Office of Disability Access is a student-, faculty-, and staff-facing position focused on advancing digital accessibility across the University of North Texas. The Digital Accessibility Specialist works directly with students with disabilities and faculty to identify, troubleshoot, and resolve digital accessibility barriers that may impact a student’s access to course materials, instructional technologies, or participation in the academic experience. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more UNT Retail Dining Services, Union Burger- Food Service Specialist The Food Service Specialist at Union Burger within UNT Retail Dining Services is responsible for delivering high-quality food and exceptional customer service in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. This position supports daily operations by preparing and serving menu items, maintaining food safety and sanitation standards, and ensuring a clean and welcoming dining area for students, faculty, staff, and guests. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff Read more Strategic Communications Coordinator The Strategic Communications Coordinator supports the successful execution of communications initiatives across the Division of University Advancement by coordinating projects, maintaining departmental workflows, and helping ensure strategic priorities move efficiently from planning through completion. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Advancement Advancement/Development Staff Read more UNT Retail Dining Services, Union Burger - Food Service Supervisor The Food Service Supervisor for Union Burger at the University of North Texas -Retail Dining Services is responsible for overseeing daily restaurant operations, ensuring exceptional customer service, and maintaining high standards of food quality, safety, and cleanliness. This role provides hands-on leadership to team members, supports staff training and development, and ensures efficient workflow during all service periods. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff Read more Sr Student & Pgrm Coordinator The position coordinates various activities to recruit, retain, mentor students to support the mission and strategic plan of the academic program. Responsible for managing the daily operations of the program, including mass communications, publications, research and interacting with students and potential students. Supervises all administrative tasks related to strategic planning, travel logistics, and recruiting. This position is essential to providing high quality coaching and training, while nurturing the development of students. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Research Administration Staff Read more Graphic Design Specialist This position is responsible for the professional, artistic design and production of impactful graphics and media content for communications and marketing materials of the College of Music, both print and digital. This work supports our efforts to enhance the Colleges reputation, build audiences for our concerts and events, and support the recruitment of our students, faculty, and staff. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Advertising/Marketing Staff Read more Asst Dir Registrar Processing This position is responsible for managing and directing daily operations of Reporting, Systems, and Testing, and overseeing process continuity for the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Contributes to the Office of the Registrar efforts to promote productivity, collaboration, and coordination within and between all sections of the office and functions as an escalation point for highly complex issues including handling advanced exceptions. This role requires direct interaction with students, former students, faculty, and staff, processing data-driven requests, developing training and ensuring compliance with a range of institutional, state, and federal regulations. This position requires a detail driven critical thinker who thrives in a fast-paced environment, is technically proficient in diverse software platforms and understands interdependencies. This position requires discernment and problem-solving to review escalations and complex and collaborative processes. Promotes and generates collaboration across teams to achieve a collective outcome and creates a unified team that get results optimizing outcomes and impact that directly affects enrollment and retention. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Enrollment Management Student Finance/Registrar Staff Read more Senior Academic Counselor This position is responsible for providing counseling to students by appraising their interests, aptitudes, and abilities to develop a career path and degree fit. This role typically provides supervision to lower level staff directly or on a project basis but may serve as an expert or point of escalation for more complex projects or issues. Counsels students on academic pursuits through the completion of degree program; connects students with available resources for academic success and personal/professional development; researches and evaluates and delivers presentations on services provided. This position is responsible for creating and implementing programs related to student success and retention. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Staff Read more Associate Registrar This position is responsible for strategic oversight of Curriculum, Scheduling, and Transfer, including planning, organizing, and ensuring continuity and continuous improvement of processes, systems, and student services including the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Involved in new initiatives with colleagues across campus related to enrollment and retention to ensure successful implementation. Oversees operations of multiple functional areas and works directly with staff for ongoing professional development and the implementation of new initiatives, and/or updated systems, policies, and processes. Advises students, parents, faculty and staff about departmental and university regulations. Requires discernment to resolve complex escalations and implement proactive solutions. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Enrollment Management Student Finance/Registrar Student Services/Student Affairs Staff Read more Sr Lab Animal Technician The Sr Lab Animal Technician provides operational and technical support for the daily functions of the Vivarium Animal Lab. Reporting to and in collaboration with the Research Animal Lab Manager, this position ensures the delivery of high-quality animal care, mentors junior husbandry staff and supports regulatory compliance across institutional and federal standards. This position provides technical expertise and guidance as a resource for supporting all research staff and animal care personnel. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Research & Innovation Research Administration Research Support - Laboratory/Non-Laboratory Staff Read more Postdoctoral Research Associate - Materials Science & Engineering This position is required to work closely with UNT faculty colleagues, and researchers at sponsoring agencies on high performance metallic materials. The position would require strong background in microstructure, mechanical properties, understanding of advanced solid state processing of metallic materials. Experience with solid state additive manufacturing of aluminum alloys is essential. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Postdoctoral Research Staff Read more Student Services Coordinator- FSL Provides support to student groups within Fraternity and Sorority Life and acts as an advisor and advocate for fraternity/sorority members. The coordinator assists the FSL unit in facilitating event planning, leadership, member development, and risk management, among other topics. The position collaborates with university departments in providing resources to the fraternity and sorority community. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Academic Advising Academic Technician Administrative/Office Support Student Services/Student Affairs Show More Show Less Staff Read more Vegan Cook Prepare and serve high-quality plant-based meals for Mean Greens, UNT's nationally acclaimed Vegan certified dining hall and the nation's first and only 100% plant-based collegiate dining hall. Responsible for preparing daily menu items, maintaining an attractive and fully stocked serving line throughout meal service, and ensuring food quality, consistency, and presentation standards are met. Monitor and maintain proper food temperatures using thermometers in accordance with Food Department policies and food safety regulations. Support a varied menu featuring globally inspired vegan cuisine, including stations such as fried rice, Vietnamese pho, Mediterranean grill, and fresh guacamole, while contributing to a positive dining experience for students and guests. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Student Affairs Food Services/Hospitality Staff Read more Program Dir CVAD Spec Initv This position provides strategic and creative leadership for the UNT CVAD Galleries, overseeing exhibitions, programming, collections, operations, and partnerships that support the College’s educational and cultural mission. The position develops and manages a dynamic exhibition program that showcases student, faculty, visiting, and professional artists while engaging the university and broader North Texas communities. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Fine Arts Staff Read more Senior Program Project Coordinator This role is the operational engine of the Murphy Center's student-facing programs. The Assistant Director manages all aspects of pitch competitions, drives marketing and outreach to maximize participation, and builds the pipeline from classroom to competition to accelerator. A key performance objective is growing the Innovate UNT and Breakthrough Ventures competitions to $100,000+ in total prize money by Year 3 while embedding competition requirements into select courses across campus. Denton, Texas, United States UNT-Provost Administrative/Office Support Advertising/Marketing Staff Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 133 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 › 1155 Union Circle #311277, Denton, Tx 76203-5017 Phone: 855.878.7650 (option #2) HRemployment@untsystem.edu Quick Links Home View All System Jobs My Se